// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 2 (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P3): the same LOCAL text pushed twice into a
// GLOBAL list of text. Before the fix, a non-fresh push value disqualified
// only the value itself, never the receiving container -- `p3Gl`'s
// element-free loop (now reachable at all once globals are tracked, per
// Critical 1) would free `p3X`'s handle twice, once per element slot.
// Critical 2's rule disqualifies the receiver too, the first time a
// non-literal/non-concat value is pushed: `p3Gl` never gets an element-free
// loop, so both slots (aliasing the one handle) are simply abandoned.
// Expected strict-mode leak count: 4 (see ../p3_dup_push.leaks) -- `p3X`'s
// text (struct box + data handle, 2 blocks; already disqualified by the
// existing local-var escape pass, since it's handed to `push` by bare
// identifier) plus `p3Gl`'s own list (struct box + backing-array handle
// holding two pointers to that one shared text handle, 2 blocks).

var p3Gl: list of text

func runP3DupPush() {
    var p3X: text = "dup"
    p3Gl.push(p3X)
    p3Gl.push(p3X)
    alert("p3 done")
}
